id: pm-gh1389
title: "GH-1389: Derive get omission receipts from emitted schedule and artifact aliases"
description: A material reminder or event rendered through the normalized schedule facet is still called omitted because the receipt inspects only top-level metadata keys. Derive inclusion from actual alias paths and preserve recovery for unselected members.
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-04T11:45:44.554Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-04T17:05:56.446Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-04T17:05:54.594Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-04T17:05:54.594Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 180
acceptance_criteria: Rendered reminders and events are never reported omitted; Narrow schedule selectors retain omissions for unselected material fields; Linked artifact aliases are measured independently; Standard brief full and selected field reads agree through SDK CLI and MCP.
goal: project management = context management
objective: Trustworthy bounded context and SDK-owned evidence
value: Agents can act on one truthful context read and preserve durable evidence
parent: pm-mpbb
risk: medium
confidence: medium
resolution: "SDK read receipts preserve material omission recovery across full-depth field selection and legacy dependencies. Isolated regression runners stop before checkout disposal, retain live workspaces on bounded shutdown refusal, settle paired failures, and stage compiled CLI artifacts only where used. Signal test readiness is published only after handler registration."
expected_result: "Truthful SDK and CLI omission recovery, genuine safe/defect verdicts and infrastructure refusal, no live child checkout deletion, deterministic signal fixture readiness, and unchanged mandatory complete-coverage and platform budgets."
actual_result: "Fifty linked tests and fifteen positive/fifteen real defect controls passed. Three actual signal cases failed before the cleanup fix and then passed; all five real runner tests passed again after the readiness correction. Hosted source head 65dedb748 passed 9715 tests plus two platform skips and all four coverage metrics on every one of 763 executable rows at 100 percent, including release scripts; Windows passed in 7m45s under its unchanged 12-minute ceiling. Node/Bun installed eighteen CLI/five SDK acceptance operations and npx/bunx passed. Fresh final-head hosted admission remains required before merge."
affected_version: 2026.10.4
